## Purpose
Provide a concise, always-available map of the Nuxt 4 (Vue 3) frontend to help contributors and AI agents quickly locate files, follow conventions, and add new features consistently.

## Entry Points and Key Config
- [nuxt.config.ts](mdc:frontend/nuxt.config.ts): SSR, route rules, modules (Tailwind, Pinia, VueUse, Element Plus, Notivue), security headers, Vite build, runtime config
- [app.vue](mdc:frontend/app.vue): Global layout, Notivue mount, global CSS import
- [tailwind.config.js](mdc:frontend/tailwind.config.js): Tailwind scan paths, theme extensions (colors, fonts)
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:frontend/tsconfig.json): Nuxt-generated TS references
- Additional docs: [FRONT_DIRECTORT_README.md](mdc:frontend/FRONT_DIRECTORT_README.md), [FRONT_FUNCTION_README.md](mdc:FRONT_FUNCTION_README.md), [FRONT_PAGE_README.md](mdc:FRONT_PAGE_README.md)

## Directory Map (overview)
```text
frontend/
├─ app.vue
├─ assets/
│  └─ css/
│     ├─ main.css
│     ├─ login/
│     └─ signup/
├─ components/
│  ├─ common/  ├─ home/
│  ├─ auth/
│  │  ├─ login/ └─ signup/
│  ├─ chat/ ├─ fortune/ └─ profile/
├─ composables/
│  ├─ api/ ├─ auth/ ├─ ui/ ├─ utils/ └─ validation/
├─ pages/
│  ├─ auth/ ├─ categories/ └─ counselor/
│  └─ index.vue, login.vue, signup.vue, chat.vue, fortune.vue, mypage.vue, profile.vue
├─ plugins/ (api.client.ts, vue-query.ts)
├─ public/ (favicon, robots.txt, site.webmanifest)
├─ types/ (auth/, common/, user/)
└─ nuxt.config.ts, tailwind.config.js, tsconfig.json, package.json
```

## Conventions
- Components: group by domain under `components/`; auto-import is enabled with `pathPrefix: false`. Use PascalCase filenames and shallow nesting where possible.
- Pages (routing): file-based routes under `pages/` (dynamic routes via `[slug].vue`). Default SSR is enabled; specific CSR/SWR/prerender rules live in `nuxt.config.ts` `routeRules`.
- Composables: place fetch/logic hooks in `composables/` with `useXxx.ts` naming. API queries in `composables/api`, validation in `composables/validation`.
- Styling: global CSS is in `assets/css/main.css` and imported in `app.vue`. Tailwind is the primary utility layer.
- Types: colocate shared TypeScript types in `types/` (e.g., `types/common/api.ts`, `types/auth/signup.ts`, `types/user/models.ts`).
- Plugins: initialize integrations under `plugins/` (e.g., `api.client.ts`, `vue-query.ts`). Remember that `*.client.ts` plugins run on client only.
- State: Pinia is enabled via `@pinia/nuxt`. If/when stores are added, follow Nuxt `stores/` convention (not present at the moment).

## Rendering and Caching (from nuxt.config.ts)
- SSR: enabled by default; page-based routing active
- Prerender (production): `/`, `/about`, `/terms`, `/privacy`
- SWR cache: `/horoscope/**` (1h)
- Realtime (no-cache): `/chat/**`
- CSR-only: `/profile/**`, `/settings/**`

## Security and Networking
- Proxy: `/api/**` → `NUXT_PROXY_TARGET`
- Security headers applied to all routes (X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, X-XSS-Protection)

## Quick How-To
- New page: add a `.vue` file under `pages/` (or nested dir)
- New UI block: add under `components/<domain>/`
- New API call: add composable under `composables/api/`
- New validation/util: add under `composables/validation` or `composables/utils`
- New types: add under `types/<area>/`
- New plugin: add under `plugins/` and restart dev server

